What is Abstraction?

Abstraction means showing only the essential details and hiding the internal implementation.
The user knows what an object does, but not necessarily how it does it.

Think about driving a car.

You only use:

Steering wheel
Brake
Accelerator

You don't need to know:

How the engine works
How fuel is injected
How the transmission changes gears

Those implementation details are hidden.

This is abstraction.
